  <Docs>
    <summary>
            Starts and inspects resilient task runs. <see cref="M:Azure.AI.AgentServer.Core.Tasks.ITaskInvoker.RunAsync``2(System.String,``0,Azure.AI.AgentServer.Core.Tasks.RunOptions,System.Threading.CancellationToken)" /> is
            the convenience that starts and awaits to completion; <see cref="M:Azure.AI.AgentServer.Core.Tasks.ITaskInvoker.StartAsync``2(System.String,``0,Azure.AI.AgentServer.Core.Tasks.RunOptions,System.Threading.CancellationToken)" />
            performs the creation round-trip and returns an awaitable handle. Both perform a
            task-storage round-trip and so are async (1:1 with Python <c>run</c>/<c>start</c>).
            </summary>
    <remarks>To be added.</remarks>
  </Docs>
